    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d643">

                <pb facs="0556" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/623.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Buckner to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 24, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s instruction through London. Shipping almost paralyzed.
                    Assigned revenues estimated not more than $3,000 monthly. Interest paid for
                    September. Receivership has $30,000 in bank. No payment to Liberian Government
                    for August. Only partial payments possible to customs and frontier force for
                    August and succeeding months. Frontier force reduced forty per cent. Financial
                    assistance from some source imperative. Receivership has asked fiscal agents for
                    loan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buckner</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
